SCOPE — please read, because this repository contains more than its own code.

1. The MIT licence above covers the SOURCE CODE in this repository: everything
   under src/, scripts/, server/, deploy/, and the build configuration.

2. It does NOT cover the DATA committed under public/data/, which is
   third-party and carries its own terms:

     public/data/MM_*/ (flood extents, exposure)
         Derived from UNOSAT products obtained via HDX, CC BY-SA.
         https://data.humdata.org/organization/unosat
     Region boundaries used during conversion
         geoBoundaries, ODbL.  https://www.geoboundaries.org/
     Impact figures
         WFP ADAM, CC BY-SA.  https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org

   Redistributing that data means honouring those licences, not this one. In
   particular CC BY-SA is a share-alike licence and MIT cannot override it.

3. Data fetched at RUN TIME is likewise not covered: NASA GIBS imagery and
   GPM IMERG rainfall, Open-Meteo forecasts (CC BY 4.0), GloFAS / Copernicus
   river discharge, OpenStreetMap via OpenFreeMap (ODbL), and EOX Sentinel-2
   cloudless. Note that EOX Sentinel-2 cloudless is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 — the NC
   is non-commercial, and it applies to that basemap regardless of this
   licence.

4. This project was rebuilt from https://github.com/shiwaku/chiba-flood-viewer,
   which publishes no licence of its own. The MIT grant above is made for the
   contributions in this repository; it cannot and does not relicense the
   original author's work, which remains under their copyright. Anyone
   intending to reuse the earliest commits in this history should seek that
   author's permission.
